VERDICT: Option A is exhausted across all three kernel variants on raw RGBA.
The chainring outer ring does NOT produce a Hough signal separable from
small/mid gear features regardless of:
  - Edge sparsity (v2a high-threshold + top-20%)
  - Argmax method (v2b proper 3D)
  - Radius band (v2c restricted to aim-prior)

Root cause confirmed: the strongest concentric feature in raw RGBA on these
photos is consistently an inner hub/spindle/BCD circle (r ~120-160px), not the
outer tooth ring.  Gradient-based Hough peaks on inner gradient density, not
outer geometric prior.

Escalation candidates:
  - **Option C (bolt-pattern symmetry)**: detect N-fold rotational symmetry
    directly via radial-gradient autocorrelation at angles 360°/N for N∈{4,5}.
    Attacks the *structural* signal Hough cannot surface (spider hole arms,
    not concentric edges).  Calibration burden similar to PAP-1078 ladder.
  - **Option D (descope Option A)**: file Option A as wontfix under PAP-758;
    re-route to PAP-1480 (joint R×tc scoring under PAP-1102 lineage) as the
    last surviving in-regime option.  Accept that escape-from-FFT-regime is
    architecturally blocked at the discriminator layer.

Recommendation: **Option C exploratory probe** (cheap, n=13 same cohort) as
the LAST forward attempt under PAP-1481 before recommending descope.  If
Option C also overlaps, PAP-1481 closes wontfix and PAP-758 has no successor
on the geometric-discriminator axis.
